role: Instance Test Gate
focus: mandatory-tests, regression-lock
extends: none

instance: navitrack-mobile-apps
code: navitrack/navitrack-mobile-apps
branch-baseline: bug-fix-oct-2026

rule: |
  Tests are mandatory for every new change in this instance.
  The app started with zero tests. That gap is closed only by keeping
  the suite in lockstep with the code.

  A task is not done when:
  - behavior changed and no test asserts the new behavior
  - pnpm test fails
  - a user journey changed (login, objects, history, events, settings,
    language) and pnpm test:e2e was not updated

where:
  unit: src/**/*.test.ts next to the module (vitest, happy-dom)
  api: msw/node, never a live fleet host
  screen: Testing Library + userEvent, I18nextProvider
  journey: e2e/*.spec.ts via playwright on port 5199

do-not:
  - Assert live map tiles.
  - Skip the test because the change "is small".
  - Commit to main. Sprint work stays on its branch.

commands:
  - pnpm test
  - pnpm test:e2e
